{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2219","id":5278004032,"node_id":"PR_kwDORcHGMc8AAAABOpfzQA","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2219","diff_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2219.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2219.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2219","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2219/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2219/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2219/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/statuses/5d72076caa2898969447d92eb77044b352e54956","number":2219,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Refs KS-2174: the two demo-seeder hint arms log the account id, not the raw email address","user":{"login":"kksecura","id":258699643,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2txew","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258699643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura","html_url":"https://github.com/kksecura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Refs KS-2174\n\nLinear ticket: https://linear.app/secuura/issue/KS-2174\n\n**BLUF:** Tier 2, log meta only, in `services/auth`. The two demo-seeder log calls in `Blockchain/Dev/services/auth/src/repositories/userRepo.ts` that carry a `hint` (`Demo user NOT seeded (no password supplied) ...`, line 1764, and `Demo user seeding skipped ...`, line 1773 at develop `43d7eae7a5f8`) wrote `email: account.email` into their meta. They now write `userId: account.id`, as PR 2216 (part 1) did for the other five seeder lines. This is part 2 of KS-2174: with PR 2216 it covers the eight raw-email log sites the ticket names. The `hint` strings, the dev-only `url` and every auth decision, token, credential and database write are unchanged.\n\n## What changes\n- **Product, `userRepo.ts` (+4 -2):** the two `email: account.email,` lines become `userId: account.id,`, each with one why-and-ticket comment line above it. `account.id` is already in scope (it is read at line 1723).\n- **The `KS-966` F2 cells, `Blockchain/Dev/services/auth/src/__tests__/ks949-platform-admin-seed-identity.test.ts`:** they found the two hint calls by `meta['email']`. They now find them by `meta['userId']` and the account id; the platform admin's id is a const added inside the F2 describe, and every changed group carries a why-and-ticket comment. A message-keyed find was not chosen: both accounts log the same message per arm, so it could not tell them apart and the cells \"the two hints are NOT the same string\" and \"both accounts are reported at all\" would have been vacuous.\n- **New cell file, `Blockchain/Dev/services/auth/src/__tests__/ks2174-demo-seeder-hint-arms-carry-no-raw-email.test.ts` (4 cells):** drives the real `seedDemoUsers` with no password supplied into three states (an id row exists, a distinct email row holds the address, nothing to remediate). Each arm cell asserts that the arm WAS reached (a cell that never reaches its line proves nothing), that no meta value holds an email-shaped string, and that the calls name both no-password accounts by id. The fourth cell is a control on the oracle. The harness is copied from PR 2216's cell file, which cannot be edited while that PR is open.\n- **Fragments:** a flow and a cheat fragment for KS-2174 part 2 under `Projects Documents/fragments/`.\n\nThe product change and the F2 edit are one change: with the product change alone, exactly four F2 cells go red (measured below), so they cannot be two PRs.\n\n## Red, green, planted (measured in this tree, from develop's blobs, one scripted run)\n- Before (develop's blobs): the new file reads 1 passed and 3 failed (the three arm cells, each past its reach assertion, failing on the leak assertion; the control passes); the ks949 file reads 31 of 31.\n- Product change only: the new file 4 of 4; the ks949 file 27 passed and 4 failed, exactly the four F2 cells that use `hintFor`.\n- Both changes: the new file 4 of 4; the ks949 file 31 of 31.\n- Planted: `email: account.email,` put back at the warn arm turns its two cells red and leaves the info cell and the control green; at the info arm it turns its one cell red and leaves the rest green. The saved bytes were restored and compared equal each time.\n\n## Overlap, and the one push\nPR 2216 (same file) and PR 2052 (the ks949 test file) are open on two of these paths. The push ran under Wednesday's conditional one-push grant, in the launching action, against each head as pinned (PR 2216 `b12dd042761d`, PR 2052 `b61674e7b763`): `git merge-tree --write-tree` rc 0 in both orders with equal trees on both targets; survival of both sides' lines (the merged `userRepo.ts` holds 7 lines with `userId: account.id`, PR 2216's 5 plus these 2); a planted edit in each target's hunk lines (develop 1754 and 1796; 538 and 578) conflicts rc 1 in both orders; twins merge rc 0. Neither PR is touched by this one.\n\n## Test plan / Test Evidence\n- **Touched:** `services/auth` only (one product file, one existing test file, one new test file) and a flow and cheat fragment pair.\n- **Ran** (Node v26.8.1, not the Node 24 LTS line; one Apple Silicon host, load1 2.2 to 3.3): the whole `services/auth` suite: before 150 files and 1,850 tests passed, after 151 files and 1,854 passed (the 1,850 plus the four new cells). The `docs-fragments.mjs check` with the pair: OK. `check:test-types`: auth 41 errors, all 41 in the baseline, 0 new. `audit:gate`: OK, 5 advisories, 5 baselined. eslint on the three source files, absolute paths: rc 0. The red, green and planted runs above.\n- **NOT run:** any other service's suite; the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, k6); Docker or the compose stack; Node 24; any live log (no production log level or log store was measured). The pre-merge acknowledgement boxes for Schemathesis and Akto are therefore NOT ticked.\n- **Migrations + config:** none.\n- **Pre-push hook:**\n\n```\nPREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE — 13/16 legs ran, 3 SKIPPED. Nothing failed.\n  legs 3 4 8 — local stack not up; you can clear this by starting it.\n  This is NOT a pass. Do not quote it as one — say which legs ran.\n```\n- Leg 14, verbatim: `shell suites: 127 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (of 127)`\n\n## Before this deploys\nNothing deploys from this PR. The change is to the `services/auth` log meta, so the new log lines appear only after the auth image is rebuilt and the service redeployed; no migration, config or secret changes, and no API, schema or data change.\n\n## Not claimed\nThe handler at `services/auth/src/routes/users.ts` line 678 (another open PR's) and the console lines in `services/auth/src/services/email.ts` are not part of the eight sites and are not changed. Other log layers (the shared error handler, request logs) and the `hint` strings are not changed either. This PR selects the ticket's remaining two sites; it does not claim the ticket's other log layers.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"